What the C actually does, which drove the translation:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- [38;5;10minitialize_test_data[0m is [38;5;10mstatic[0m and never called, so [38;5;10mnode_count[0m stays 0 for the library's entire lifetime and [38;5;10mfind_node_by_id[0m always returns NULL. Modes 1, 2, and 4 therefore always take their early-return error paths (18, 34, 66), mode 3 is the only live computation, and anything else returns 130. I reproduced this rather than wiring up the initializer.[0m[0m
- No namespace macros in [38;5;10minclude/lib.h[0m, so the linker symbol is plain [38;5;10mjumpnode[0m (confirmed with [38;5;10mnm[0m).[0m[0m
- Octal literals throughout ([38;5;10m0100[0m, [38;5;10m0377[0m, [38;5;10m020[0m, …) were converted to Rust [38;5;10m0o[0m forms, not decimal.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
I kept [38;5;10madd_node[0m, [38;5;10minitialize_test_data[0m, [38;5;10mprocess_backward[0m, and the unused status constants in the translation as [38;5;10m#[allow(dead_code)][0m so the file stays a faithful mirror of the C. To confirm those dormant paths are also correct, I temporarily exposed the initializer in throwaway copies of both the C and Rust (outside [38;5;10mc_src/[0m and outside the deliverable) and compared with populated node state: 7,128 of 7,191 cases identical.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The 63 exceptions are all mode 2 with negative [38;5;10mdepth[0m. There, [38;5;10mprocess_backward[0m computes [38;5;10mstart = array + start_offset[0m with a negative offset and sums backward from [38;5;10mtemp_array[15][0m down past [38;5;10mtemp_array[0][0m, reading uninitialized stack memory before the array. This is undefined behavior, and the C is not self-consistent about it either — [38;5;10mgcc -O0[0m and [38;5;10mgcc -O2[0m disagree with each other on those same inputs, so there is no behavior to match. The path is unreachable in the shipped library anyway, since mode 2 always returns 34 before reaching it.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Two other deliberate choices: integer arithmetic uses [38;5;10mwrapping_*[0m (C signed overflow is UB; wrapping matches what gcc emits in practice), and [38;5;10msafe_double_to_int[0m clamps before the cast exactly as the C does, so the [38;5;10mas i32[0m conversion never hits a range where Rust's saturation would diverge from C's truncation.[0m[0m
